  "body": "In `authority state`, the pointer is specified to decrement, and only change state on:\r\n\r\n- EOL\r\n\r\n- U+002F (/)\r\n\r\n- U+003F (?)\r\n\r\n- U+0023 (#)\r\n\r\nI'm wondering why the symbols `/`, `?`, and `#` are used in this section because the symbols `?` and `#` can be used in passwords.\r\n\r\nFor the implementation of the `authority state`, a url such as: \r\n\r\n`scheme://root:pass#word@example.com`\r\n\r\nWould result in undefined behavior, as the octothorp should not move the parser into the fragment state.",
